      "extract_value": "This subsection reports a male sample of n = 165 and psychometric results for the scale: KMO = .95 and Bartlett's test of sphericity was significant (\u03c72(45) = 1568.24, p < .001), indicating adequate factorability. A single factor had an eigenvalue of 7.08 explaining 70.8% of variance, item loadings ranged .80\u2013.90, and internal consistency was high (Cronbach \u03b1 = .96).",
